{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 65, :comments ["<b>Then HaShem awoke</b> — Scripture speaks counter to the design of the Philistines, who seized the place of the Glory. Or it is by way of parable, because the might of the Glory was not seen when the Ark was taken, and now the reviler mocks Him, for he trusts in his strength. And some say: the reviler is the drunkard when the deep sleep falls."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :register {:fixes 1}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:21.098728702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}